# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:admissionInformation.title/short
msgid "1. Document details, admission and discharge"
msgstr "1. Сведения о документе, поступление и выписка"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:admissionInformation.code/short
msgid "Medical-card number, full name, age, address, workplace, admission date and time, referring organization, ward, blood group, Rh factor, laboratory tests, allergies, diagnoses on admission and discharge, complications, operations, discharge date and outcome"
msgstr "Номер медицинской карты, ФИО, возраст, адрес, место работы, дата и время поступления, направившая организация, палата, группа крови, резус-фактор, лабораторные исследования, аллергии, диагнозы при поступлении и выписке, осложнения, операции, дата выписки и исход"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:admissionInformation.entry/short
msgid "Patient, stay, organizations, laboratory results, allergies, diagnoses and operations"
msgstr "Пациентка, пребывание, организации, результаты анализов, аллергии, диагнозы и операции"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:medicalAndObstetricHistory.title/short
msgid "2. Medical and obstetric history"
msgstr "2. Общий и акушерский анамнез"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:medicalAndObstetricHistory.code/short
msgid "Occupation, general diseases, spouse's health, menstrual, sexual and gynecological history, previous pregnancies, deliveries and abortions, epidemiological history"
msgstr "Профессия, общие заболевания, здоровье мужа, менструальный, половой и гинекологический анамнез, предыдущие беременности, роды и аборты, эпидемиологический анамнез"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:medicalAndObstetricHistory.entry/short
msgid "Spouse, history observations, occupation, past diseases and operations, history questionnaire"
msgstr "Муж, наблюдения анамнеза, профессия, перенесённые заболевания и операции, опросник анамнеза"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:currentPregnancy.title/short
msgid "3. Course of this pregnancy and general examination"
msgstr "3. Течение данной беременности и общий осмотр"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:currentPregnancy.code/short
msgid "Prenatal visits, complications of this pregnancy, general condition, height, weight, blood pressure, pulse, temperature, organ systems"
msgstr "Пренатальные визиты, осложнения данной беременности, общее состояние, рост, вес, артериальное давление, пульс, температура, системы органов"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:currentPregnancy.entry/short
msgid "Pregnancy course and general examination findings"
msgstr "Течение беременности и данные общего осмотра"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:obstetricExamination.title/short
msgid "4. Obstetric examination and fetal assessment"
msgstr "4. Акушерское исследование и оценка плода"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:obstetricExamination.code/short
msgid "Fundal height, abdominal circumference, pelvimetry, gravidity and parity, and for each fetus: lie, position, presentation, heart sounds, heart rate, estimated weight"
msgstr "Высота стояния дна матки, окружность живота, пельвиометрия, число беременностей и родов, а для каждого плода: положение, позиция, предлежание, сердцебиение, ЧСС, предполагаемая масса"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:obstetricExamination.entry/short
msgid "Maternal measurements and one set of fetal observations per fetus"
msgstr "Измерения у матери и отдельный набор наблюдений для каждого плода"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:laborCourse.title/short
msgid "5. Course of labor"
msgstr "5. Течение родов"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:laborCourse.code/short
msgid "Onset of labor, rupture of membranes, amniotic fluid, cervical dilation, pain relief and its effect, delivery, episiotomy, blood loss, durations of labor and its stages"
msgstr "Начало родов, излитие околоплодных вод, околоплодные воды, раскрытие шейки матки, обезболивание и его эффект, родоразрешение, эпизиотомия, кровопотеря, продолжительность родов и их периодов"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:laborCourse.entry/short
msgid "Labor observations, delivery procedures and administered medication"
msgstr "Наблюдения в родах, процедуры родоразрешения и введённые препараты"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:newbornDeliveryRecord.title/short
msgid "6. Newborn delivery record"
msgstr "6. Сведения о новорождённом"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:newbornDeliveryRecord.code/short
msgid "For each newborn: time of birth, sex, born alive or dead, weight, length, head and chest circumference, condition, Apgar scores, eye prophylaxis; placenta, membranes and cord"
msgstr "Для каждого новорождённого: время рождения, пол, родился живым или мёртвым, масса, длина, окружность головы и груди, состояние, оценка по Апгар, профилактика гонобленнореи; послед, оболочки и пуповина"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:newbornDeliveryRecord.entry/short
msgid "Each newborn and their birth observations and procedures"
msgstr "Каждый новорождённый, наблюдения и процедуры при рождении"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.Composition.section:newbornDeliveryRecord.entry/definition
msgid "Include a separate UZCorePatient for each newborn. When PINFL is absent, use the newborn's DMED medical-card number in Patient.identifier[healthCardId], using the UZ Core HC identifier system. Individual measurements and Apgar assessments reference that newborn as Observation.subject; delivery-wide counts reference the mother. Reuse the same patient identity in Form 097 and add PINFL to that identity when available."
msgstr "Include a separate UZCorePatient for each newborn. When PINFL is absent, use the newborn's DMED medical-card number in Patient.identifier[healthCardId], using the UZ Core HC identifier system. Individual measurements and Apgar assessments reference that newborn as Observation.subject; delivery-wide counts reference the mother. Reuse the same patient identity in Form 097 and add PINFL to that identity when available."

